-- title:
--   §2 and p.18 — realization-based repeated play, the past σ-algebra, and the averages $\overline Q_t$, $\widehat Q_t$
-- statement:
--   Let $(\Omega,\mathcal F,\mu)$ be a probability space and $I_t,J_t\in\{0,1\}$ the actions realized by players 1 and 2 in round $t$. Let
--   $$
--   \mathcal F_t:=\sigma\big((I_s,J_s)_{s=1}^{t-1}\big)
--   $$
--   be the information of the rounds before round $t$. Given self-agnostic strategies $f$ of player 1 and $g$ of player 2, the processes **carry the play** of $(f,g)$ if $I_t,J_t$ are measurable, the mixed strategies are the strategies evaluated on the realized past,
--   $$
--   P_t=f_t\big((J)^{t-1}\big),\qquad Q_t=g_t\big((I)^{t-1}\big),
--   $$
--   and conditionally on $\mathcal F_t$ the actions are independent with $I_t\sim\mathrm{Ber}(P_t)$ and $J_t\sim\mathrm{Ber}(Q_t)$, i.e. almost surely
--   $$
--   \Pr(I_t=1\mid\mathcal F_t)=P_t,\quad \Pr(J_t=1\mid\mathcal F_t)=Q_t,\quad \Pr(I_t=1,J_t=1\mid\mathcal F_t)=P_tQ_t .
--   $$
--   Players see only realized actions, never the opponent's mixed strategy. The file also defines the time-average of player 2's mixed strategies and the empirical average of player 2's actions,
--   $$
--   \overline Q_t=\frac1t\sum_{s=1}^tQ_s,\qquad \widehat Q_t=\frac1t\sum_{s=1}^tJ_s .
--   $$
--
--   This is the probabilistic model of all statements about the joint dynamics (Lemma 3.7, Eq. (3.26), Theorem 3.4).
--
--   **Formalization Note** Rounds are indexed from $0$ in Lean: the past of Lean round $n$ is $\sigma((I_k,J_k):k<n)$, which never contains round $n$ itself. The three conditional expectations determine the conditional law of $(I_t,J_t)$ on $\{0,1\}^2$ as $\mathrm{Ber}(P_t)\otimes\mathrm{Ber}(Q_t)$. The model is inhabited by non-degenerate plays (checked in Lean for $P_t=Q_t=1/2$ on an infinite product space).
-- source:
--   Muthukumar, Phade, Sahai, On the Impossibility of Convergence of Mixed Strategies with Optimal No-Regret Learning, arXiv:2012.02125v3, §2 pp.5–6 (I, J, P̂, Q̂, P̄, Q̄; independent implementation of mixed strategies), p.18 (filtration F_t, J_t ∼ Ber(Q_t))

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_NoRegretLastIterate_Strategy

namespace NoRegretLastIterate

open MeasureTheory

/-- arXiv:2012.02125v3, p.18: the σ-algebra `F_t := σ((I_s, J_s)_{s=1}^{t−1})` generated by the
realized actions of the rounds before the current one.

**Formalization Note** In Lean indexing `pastSigma I J n = σ((I k, J k) : k < n)`: the past of
Lean round `n` (paper round `n + 1`), never including round `n` itself. -/
def pastSigma {Ω : Type*} (I J : ℕ → Ω → Fin 2) (n : ℕ) : MeasurableSpace Ω :=
  ⨆ k ∈ Finset.range n, MeasurableSpace.comap (fun ω => (I k ω, J k ω)) inferInstance

/-- arXiv:2012.02125v3, §2, pp.5–6 and p.18: `(Ω, μ, I, J)` carries the *realization-based play*
of the self-agnostic strategies `F₁` (player 1) and `F₂` (player 2). The realized actions
`I_t, J_t ∈ {0, 1}` are measurable; in every round the mixed strategies are
`P_t = F₁(J^{t−1})` and `Q_t = F₂(I^{t−1})`, functions of the realized past; and conditionally on
the past `F_t`, the actions are independent with `I_t ∼ Ber(P_t)` and `J_t ∼ Ber(Q_t)`
("since the two players will implement their mixed strategies independently, the random
variables I and J will be independent", p.5; "J_t ∼ Ber(Q_t)", p.18).

**Formalization Note** The conditional law of `(I_t, J_t) ∈ {0,1}²` given `F_t` is pinned down by
the three conditional expectations `E[1{I_t=1} | F_t] = P_t`, `E[1{J_t=1} | F_t] = Q_t` and
`E[1{I_t=1, J_t=1} | F_t] = P_t Q_t` (almost surely), i.e. it is `Ber(P_t) ⊗ Ber(Q_t)`. Lean
round `n` is paper round `n + 1`; `F₁ n` sees `J 0, …, J (n−1)`. -/
def IsPlay {Ω : Type*} [MeasurableSpace Ω] (μ : Measure Ω)
    (F₁ F₂ : (n : ℕ) → (Fin n → Fin 2) → ℝ) (I J : ℕ → Ω → Fin 2) : Prop :=
  (∀ n, Measurable (I n)) ∧ (∀ n, Measurable (J n)) ∧
  ∀ n,
    (μ[fun ω => bit (I n ω) | pastSigma I J n] =ᵐ[μ]
      fun ω => F₁ n (fun k : Fin n => J k ω)) ∧
    (μ[fun ω => bit (J n ω) | pastSigma I J n] =ᵐ[μ]
      fun ω => F₂ n (fun k : Fin n => I k ω)) ∧
    (μ[fun ω => bit (I n ω) * bit (J n ω) | pastSigma I J n] =ᵐ[μ]
      fun ω => F₁ n (fun k : Fin n => J k ω) * F₂ n (fun k : Fin n => I k ω))

/-- arXiv:2012.02125v3, §2, p.6: `Q̄_t := (1/t) Σ_{s=1}^t Q_s`, the time-average of player 2's
mixed strategies `Q_s = F₂(I^{s−1})` along the realized play (Lean rounds `0, …, t − 1`). -/
noncomputable def avgMixed {Ω : Type*} (F₂ : (n : ℕ) → (Fin n → Fin 2) → ℝ)
    (I : ℕ → Ω → Fin 2) (t : ℕ) (ω : Ω) : ℝ :=
  (∑ n ∈ Finset.range t, F₂ n (fun k : Fin n => I k ω)) / t

/-- arXiv:2012.02125v3, §2, p.5: `Q̂_t := (1/t) Σ_{s=1}^t J_s`, the empirical average of player 2's
realized actions (Lean rounds `0, …, t − 1`). -/
noncomputable def avgAct {Ω : Type*} (J : ℕ → Ω → Fin 2) (t : ℕ) (ω : Ω) : ℝ :=
  (∑ n ∈ Finset.range t, bit (J n ω)) / t

end NoRegretLastIterate


